                                                "sense_id": "9a225bd0-2996-3e15-901c-6dba5fc10bf5",
                                                "text": "To the preparation, then: vegetables softened in butter, lots of Guinness, thick chunks of second-cut brisket — breast deckle, as it’s called in some of New York’s better precincts (where trotter gear, by the by, is known as trayf city)."
